<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21233] lfs: report the volatile FID in mirror extend/migrate --stats output</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21233</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lfs mirror extend&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;lfs migrate&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;lfs migrate -m&lt;/tt&gt;-to-DoM copy the data through an open-unlinked volatile file. The new layout is then merged or swapped into the original file. This volatile file has its own FID. It has no name, so &lt;tt&gt;lfs fid2path&lt;/tt&gt; can't resolve it, and it is gone once the command finishes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a result, the OSTs record every write the copy makes under a FID that nothing else ever reports. Tools that watch OST access (for example readers of the OFD access log, or tiering and heat tracking) see a large burst of writes to an unknown FID. They can't tell this I/O apart from application I/O.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;--stats&lt;/tt&gt; already prints a YAML progress stream for whoever runs the copy. &lt;br/&gt;
Proposal: print the volatile FID once, right after the file-name header and before any data is copied:{&lt;tt&gt;}&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
/mnt/lustre/dir/file:
- { volatile_fid: &lt;span class="code-quote"&gt;"[0x200000401:0x2:0x0]"&lt;/span&gt; }
- { seconds: 1, rmbps: 16, wmbps: 16, copied: 16, total: 32, pct: 50% }&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</description>
